ercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.2453,"playId":"401869950316","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.2534,"playId":"401869950320","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.2273,"playId":"401869950323","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.1987,"playId":"401869950326","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.2196,"playId":"401869950332","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.2269,"playId":"401869950337","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.2192,"playId":"401869950341","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.1922,"playId":"401869950353","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.137,"playId":"401869950420","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.1755,"playId":"401869950359","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.1795,"playId":"401869950363","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.1527,"playId":"401869950366","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.1488,"playId":"401869950371","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.132,"playId":"401869950376","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.1346,"playId":"401869950381","tiePercentage":0}],"gameInfo":{"venue":{"id":"3918","guid":"446c5fc1-ec35-39e6-be2b-b948e2a37a54","fullName":"S.B. Ballard Stadium","address":{"city":"Norfolk","state":"VA","zipCode":"23508","country":"USA"},"grass":false,"images":[{"href":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/venues/college-football/day/interior/3918.jpg","width":2000,"height":1125,"alt":"","rel":["full","day","interior"]}]},"attendance":17912},"article":{"headline":"Turner Helton, Tripp Bryant lead Georgia Southern to 23-15 victory over Old Dominion","description":"— Turner Helton threw a touchdown pass and Tripp Bryant kicked three field goals to guide Georgia Southern to a 23-15 victory over Old Dominion on Thursday night.","story":"NORFOLK, Va. -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4912238/turner-helton\" target=\"_new\">Turner Helton</a> threw a touchdown pass and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5238178/tripp-bryant\" target=\"_new\">Tripp Bryant</a> kicked three field goals to guide Georgia Southern to a 23-15 victory over Old Dominion on Thursday night.\n\n\r\n              Helton completed 23 of 30 passes for 205 yards for Georgia Southern (3-4, 2-1 Sun Belt Conference). <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4685348/terrance-gibbs\" target=\"_new\">Terrance Gibbs</a> had a touchdown run and a touchdown catch.\n\n\r\n              Old Dominion (2-5, 1-3) grabbed a 7-0 lead when <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5193346/quinn-henicle\" target=\"_new\">Quinn Henicle</a> connected with tight end <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4832875/leon-haughton-jr\" target=\"_new\">Leon Haughton Jr</a>. for a 20-yard touchdown at the end of an 11-play, 75-yard drive to start the game.\n\n\r\n              Gibbs had an 11-yard touchdown run as Georgia Southern answered with a 12-play, 75-yard drive on its first possession to tie it 7-all after one quarter.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5091788/aaron-sears\" target=\"_new\">Aaron Sears</a> recovered a fumble by <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4922993/devin-roche\" target=\"_new\">Devin Roche</a> and the Eagles turned it into a 33-yard field goal by Bryant for a 10-7 lead early in the second quarter.\n\n\r\n              Bryant added a 43-yarder with 4:43 left and a 31-yarder in the final minute for a 16-7 advantage at halftime.\n\n\r\n              Helton tossed an 11-yard touchdown pass to Gibbs at the end of an 11-play drive and the Eagles led 23-7 with 4:29 left in the third quarter.\n\n\r\n              Backup <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/3957236/ryan-huff\" target=\"_new\">Ryan Huff</a> threw a short pass to <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4921111/tj-johnson\" target=\"_new\">TJ Johnson</a> and he turned it into a 71-yard touchdown. The Monarchs added the two-point conversion to trail by eight with 10 minutes remaining but got no closer.\n\n\r\n              Henicle had 86 yards on 6-for-10 passing and Huff completed 9 of 14 for 115 yards for Old Dominion. The Monarchs managed only 65 yards on 32 rushes.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Georgia Southern: Hosts Appalachian State on Oct. 31.\n\n\r\n              Old Dominion: At Louisiana Tech on Oct. 24.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"https://apnews.com/newsletters\">Sign up for Top 25 poll alerts here</a>. Visit <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/ap-top-25-college-football-poll\">the Top 25 here</a> and see AP’s full <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/college-football\">college football coverage here.</a>","published":"2026-10-16T03:17:26Z"}}